The difference: the DOM client's fresh-render grid cell wrapper is `<div><span data-pathland-id=7>...` (no justify-self/align-self), but the SSR canonical is `<div style:align-self:start;justify-self:start><span...`. 

The `applyLayout` should have set the wrapper's justifySelf/alignSelf. But in the fresh render path (`renderFresh`), does `applyLayout` run? The `applyLayout` is called at the end of `applyBatch` (line 268 area). For the fresh-DOM render, applyBatch is called, so applyLayout should run and set the wrapper styles. But the wrapper has no style at all — meaning applyLayout's grid branch didn't run, OR the grid container's `el.style.alignItems` is empty and the token default "start" should still set justifySelf/alignSelf = "start" on the wrapper.

Wait — the wrapper has NO inline style (`<div>` with nothing). applyLayout's grid branch sets `w.style.justifySelf` and `w.style.alignSelf`. For a non-FILL cell (the "Cell" text), `fillsAxis(w, true, false)` → false → `w.style.justifySelf = token`. token = `el.style.alignItems || "start"` = "start". So the wrapper should get `justify-self:start;align-self:start`. But it didn't. 

Why? Possibly applyLayout's Phase 1 loop checks `if (!PROPAGATING.has(comp)) continue;` — the grid is NOT in PROPAGATING (only stacks + ZStack)! Look at Phase 1:
```ts
for (const el of els) {
  const comp = componentByNode.get(el) ?? 0;
  if (!PROPAGATING.has(comp)) {
    continue;
